# AGENTS.md

Project name: {{project_name}}
Primary language: Python {{python_version}}

Canonical source for how AI coding agents work in this repository.
`CLAUDE.md`, `GEMINI.md`, `.cursor/rules/agents.mdc`, `.windsurf/rules/agents.md`,
`.clinerules/agents.md`, `.kiro/steering/agents.md`, and `.github/copilot-instructions.md`
all point back here — edit this file, not those. Run `scripts/check-agent-sync.sh`
if you're unsure whether one of them has drifted.

## 1. Three layers

- **Source** — code, tests, specs, ADRs, commit/PR history. Ground truth. Agents
  read it; they don't rewrite it to make the docs look right.
- **Docs (the wiki)** — `docs/`. A synthesis of the source, organized per Diátaxis
  (§4), kept current by `doc-librarian`.
- **Schema** — this file plus `skills/`. Defines how agents behave and how the
  other two layers stay healthy. Co-evolves with the project — see §6.

## 2. Coding guardrails

Full detail: `skills/minimal-by-default/SKILL.md`.

Before adding code, work down this ladder and stop at the first rung that solves
the problem: *does this need to exist → stdlib → platform feature → an
already-installed dependency → one line → the minimum custom code that works.*

Never shortcut: trust-boundary validation, data-loss handling, security,
accessibility, or correctness under failure/concurrency. If a shortcut is taken
deliberately elsewhere, mark it: `// TODO(minimal): <what was skipped, and when
to revisit>`.

## 3. Plan, then build, then review

Full detail: `skills/plan-before-build/SKILL.md`, `skills/review-before-ship/SKILL.md`.

For non-trivial work (new features, multi-file changes, anything with more than
one reasonable approach): state the plan briefly, argue against it, *then* write
code. After writing it, do one adversarial pass on the diff before calling the
task done. Scale the ceremony to the task — a one-line fix needs neither step
written out.

## 4. Documentation system

Full detail: `skills/doc-librarian/SKILL.md`. Framework: [diataxis.fr](https://diataxis.fr).

| Content helps someone... | ...who is... | Goes in             |
| ------------------------ | ------------ | ------------------- |
| do something             | learning     | `docs/tutorials/`   |
| do something             | working      | `docs/how-to/`      |
| look something up        | working      | `docs/reference/`   |
| understand something     | learning     | `docs/explanation/` |

`docs/index.md` catalogs every page; `docs/log.md` is an append-only history
(`## [YYYY-MM-DD] <ingest|edit|lint> | <title>`). Three operations keep it
healthy: **ingest** new material into the right page(s) and update the
index/log; **query** the index before searching page-by-page, and file good
answers back as pages; **lint** periodically for orphan pages, stale claims,
and mode-mixing.

## 5. Skills

| Skill                | Triggers on                        | Default |
| -------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------- |
| `minimal-by-default` | any implementation work            | on      |
| `plan-before-build`  | non-trivial work, before coding    | on      |
| `review-before-ship` | non-trivial diffs, before shipping | on      |
| `doc-librarian`      | writing/updating/auditing docs     | on      |
| `concise-output`     | only if asked, or enabled below    | **off** |

To turn `concise-output` on for this project, change its line above to `on`.

## 6. Keeping this file alive

This file should get better as the project teaches you things — if the same
mistake gets corrected twice, write the rule here instead of re-explaining it
next session. Give changes to this file slightly more scrutiny than a docs
page: every future agent session reads it.

## 7. Adding a new agent

New tool reads a different rule-file location? Add a one-file pointer for it
next to the others (copy the format of any existing adapter), add it to the
list in `scripts/check-agent-sync.sh`, and it's covered.

